# Civil Liberties, Libraries, and Computers

**Authors:** Crooks, Joyce

## Abstract
The civil liberties issues involved in the keeping of public records certainly arose prior to the use of computers, but automated information systems have, beyond any question, aggravated those issues involved in all areas of application and have made the need for legal protection crucial, if we are not to see a synergistic development of national dossiers in our time. (Author)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ131268

